1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:07,700
In early 2008, a Danish household paid 26 cents for a kilowatt-hour of electricity.

2
00:00:08,100 --> 00:00:10,900
For years, the price crept up slowly.

3
00:00:13,300 --> 00:00:17,668
Then, in the second half of 2022, gas prices soared,

4
00:00:17,668 --> 00:00:24,725
and Danish electricity hit 59 cents a kilowatt-hour. More than twice the 2008 price.

5
00:00:25,125 --> 00:00:30,500
The EU average peaked later, in early 2024, at 29 cents.

6
00:00:30,900 --> 00:00:37,441
Now Denmark has cut its electricity tax almost to zero, and it pays 24 cents.

7
00:00:37,441 --> 00:00:40,075
Less than the EU average of 28.

8
00:00:40,475 --> 00:00:44,750
The whole story of Europe's power prices is in our full video.
